{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.PosDef","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Matrix.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.PosSemidefTraceZero"],"declarations":33,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.StrictComplementarityPair.inactive_dual_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.StrictComplementarityPair.inactive_dual_zero","kind":"theorem","line":244,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L244-L244","doc":"Off the active set, the dual variable is exactly zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.StrictComplementarityPair.active_dual_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.StrictComplementarityPair.active_dual_pos","kind":"theorem","line":242,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L242-L242","doc":"On the active set, the dual variable is strictly positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.StrictComplementarityPair.active","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.StrictComplementarityPair.active","kind":"def","line":240,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L240-L240","doc":"The active set: indices where the dual variable is positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.StrictComplementarityPair.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.StrictComplementarityPair.mk","kind":"ctor","line":237,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L237-L237","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.StrictComplementarityPair.toStrongDualityPair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.StrictComplementarityPair.toStrongDualityPair","kind":"def","line":237,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L237-L244","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.StrictComplementarityPair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.StrictComplementarityPair","kind":"structure","line":219,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L219-L244","doc":"**Strict-complementarity certificate.**\n\nStrengthens `StrongDualityPair` with the active/inactive\npartition of the constraint indices.  An index `i` is \"active\"\niff its dual variable `ystar i` is strictly positive (constraint\nis binding); otherwise it is \"inactive\" with `ystar i = 0`.\n\nConcrete fields:\n* `active : Set ι` — the active set\n* `active_dual_pos` — `∀ i ∈ active, 0 < ystar i`\n* `inactive_dual_zero` — `∀ i ∉ active, ystar i = 0`\n\nThe \"strict\" qualifier means the dichotomy is sharp: there is\nno ambiguous case where both `ystar i > 0` and the slack is\npositive.  This is the Todd 2001 §3.4 / Boyd-Vandenberghe §5.5\nformulation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.strong_duality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.strong_duality","kind":"theorem","line":201,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L201-L208","doc":"**Strong duality** (per-instance form). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.HasStrongDuality.pair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.HasStrongDuality.pair","kind":"theorem","line":199,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L199-L199","doc":"A strong-duality pair exists. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.HasStrongDuality.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.HasStrongDuality.mk","kind":"ctor","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L196-L196","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.HasStrongDuality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.HasStrongDuality","kind":"class","line":188,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L188-L199","doc":"**Strong-duality typeclass**: witnesses that an SDP satisfies\nthe primal-dual identity (Slater's condition + strong duality\nfor convex problems, Boyd-Vandenberghe §5.2.3 + §5.3). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.StrongDualityPair.obj_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.StrongDualityPair.obj_eq","kind":"theorem","line":186,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L186-L186","doc":"Zero duality gap: primal and dual objectives agree. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.StrongDualityPair.dual_feas","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.StrongDualityPair.dual_feas","kind":"theorem","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L184-L184","doc":"Dual feasibility: the dual slack `T - Σ ystar_i A_i` is PSD. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.StrongDualityPair.primal_feas","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.StrongDualityPair.primal_feas","kind":"theorem","line":182,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L182-L182","doc":"Primal feasibility witness. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.StrongDualityPair.ystar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.StrongDualityPair.ystar","kind":"def","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L180-L180","doc":"Dual-optimal point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.StrongDualityPair.Φstar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.StrongDualityPair.Φstar","kind":"def","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L178-L178","doc":"Primal-optimal point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.StrongDualityPair.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.StrongDualityPair.mk","kind":"ctor","line":176,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L176-L176","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.StrongDualityPair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.StrongDualityPair","kind":"structure","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L160-L186","doc":"**Strong-duality pair** at an optimum.\n\nA primal point `Φstar`, a dual point `ystar`, and the two facts that\nmake them a primal-dual optimal pair: `Φstar` is primal-feasible,\nthe dual slack `S(ystar) = T - Σ ystar_i A_i` is PSD (dual\nfeasibility), and the two objectives agree (zero duality gap).\n\nUntil 2026-11-15 the last two fields were `True`, on the stated\nground that PSD-ness \"cannot be expressed without `[Fintype ι]` and\n`R := ℝ`\".  Only the first half of that was right: `Matrix.PosSemidef`\nis defined over any `CommRing R` with `PartialOrder` and `StarRing`,\nwhich this file already assumes for `IsFeasible`.  `[Fintype ι]` is\nthe only extra input, and it is carried here.  `RealStrongDualityPair`\n(`QOU.MathlibExt.SDPRealUniqueness`) states the same two fields at\n`R := ℝ`; see `StrongDualityPair.toReal`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.SDPPrimal.dualSlack_trace_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.SDPPrimal.dualSlack_trace_eq","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L124-L147","doc":"**Key algebraic identity**: `tr(S(y) · Φ) = objAt Φ -\ndualObjAt y` for any feasible `Φ`.  Combines\n`Matrix.trace_add` / `_smul` / `_sub` with feasibility\n(`tr(A_i · Φ) = b_i`).\n\nPROOF: linearity of trace + feasibility constraints. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.SDPPrimal.dualObjAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.SDPPrimal.dualObjAt","kind":"def","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L120-L122","doc":"**Dual objective value** at a dual point `y`: `Σ_i y_i · b_i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.SDPPrimal.dualSlack","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.SDPPrimal.dualSlack","kind":"def","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L115-L118","doc":"**Dual slack matrix** `S(y) := T - Σ_i y_i · A_i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.SDPDual.y","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.SDPDual.y","kind":"def","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L102-L102","doc":"The dual variables, one per primal equality constraint. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.SDPDual.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.SDPDual.mk","kind":"ctor","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L100-L100","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.SDPDual","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.SDPDual","kind":"structure","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L98-L102","doc":"**Dual SDP** derived from the primal: maximise `Σ b_i y_i` over\n`y : ι → R` subject to `T - Σ y_i A_i ⪰ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.SDPPrimal.objAt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.SDPPrimal.objAt","kind":"def","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L94-L96","doc":"**Primal-feasible objective value** at a given feasible point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.isFeasible_of_emptyConstraints","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.isFeasible_of_emptyConstraints","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L84-L92","doc":"**Empty-constraint feasibility** — proved theorem. With no\nequality constraints, every PSD matrix is feasible. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.feasible_of_strictlyFeasible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.feasible_of_strictlyFeasible","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L75-L82","doc":"**Strictly feasible implies feasible** — proved theorem.\nA positive-definite matrix is positive-semidefinite, so any\nSlater-witness is automatically a feasible point. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.SDPPrimal.IsStrictlyFeasible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.SDPPrimal.IsStrictlyFeasible","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L68-L73","doc":"**Slater-strict feasibility**: there exists a positive-definite\n`Φ ≻ 0` (not just PSD) satisfying every equality constraint. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.SDPPrimal.IsFeasible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.SDPPrimal.IsFeasible","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L64-L66","doc":"**Feasibility predicate** for an SDP candidate `Φ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.SDPPrimal.rhs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.SDPPrimal.rhs","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L60-L60","doc":"Right-hand sides of equality constraints. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.SDPPrimal.constraint","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.SDPPrimal.constraint","kind":"def","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L58-L58","doc":"Equality-constraint operators (one per index `i : ι`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.SDPPrimal.cost","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.SDPPrimal.cost","kind":"def","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L56-L56","doc":"The cost operator. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.SDPPrimal.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.SDPPrimal.mk","kind":"ctor","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L54-L54","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.SDPPrimal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.SDP.SDPPrimal","kind":"structure","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/SDP.lean#L49-L60","doc":"**Primal SDP problem data.**\n\nA semidefinite program: minimise `⟨T, Φ⟩ := tr(T · Φ)` over\n`Φ ⪰ 0` subject to equality constraints `tr(A_i · Φ) = b_i`\nfor each `i : ι`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}